{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"by8uzr12m","tool_use_id":"toolu_01SxkbGVwf6MDzQJU6osVjUu","status":"completed","output_file":"/tmp/claude-441489/-scratch-users-kushinm-auto-psych-outer-loop-live-runs-run1-repo/842b0e3e-776f-4b34-addc-274cf9e6d4dc/tasks/by8uzr12m.output","summary":"Background command \"cd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop; D=iter_2/candidate_0\ncat > $D/hypothesis.md << 'EOF'\nTo compare two sequences people must hold both in working memory, and each person has their own memory capacity: once a sequence's length approaches or exceeds that capacity, the flips are encoded noisily and the comparison is blurred, so a low-capacity person follows their impression of which sequence looks more random sharply for short pairs but only weakly for long ones, while a high-capacity person is equally decisive at every length. The impression itself is the current best judgement (personal ideal switching rate and sensitivity with lenience toward over-alternation, personal weights on imbalance and the longest streak, shared weights on the final streak, mirror symmetry, run-length variety, the most lopsided stretch and complement symmetry, and a personal guessing rate); the personal capacity predicts that people differ in how consistently they agree with the majority, and that these differences are concentrated on long pairs.\nEOF\necho personal_memory_capacity_blur > $D/model_name.txt\npython3 - << 'EOF'\nsrc = open(\"models/complement_symmetry_aversion.py\").read()\ndoc_end = src.index('\"\"\"', 3) + 3\nnewdoc = '''\"\"\"Personal working-memory capacity blurs comparisons of long sequences.\n\nTo compare two sequences people hold both in working memory; each person has\ntheir own capacity, and as the number of flips grows past it the encoding gets\nnoisy, so the same difference in apparent randomness decides the choice less\nsharply: the comparison is divided by sqrt(1 + (n / K_i)^2), with K_i the\nperson's capacity (in flips) drawn from a population. The impression itself is\nthe current best judgement (personal ideal switching rate and sensitivity with\nan asymmetric tolerance, personal weights on imbalance and the longest run,\nshared weights on the final run, mirror symmetry, run-length variety, the most\nlopsided stretch and complement symmetry, and a personal lapse rate).\n\"\"\"'''\nsrc = newdoc + src[doc_end:]\nsrc = src.replace('''        \"antisym_b\": complement_symmetric(b),\n    }''', '''        \"antisym_b\": complement_symmetric(b),\n        \"seq_len\": float(len(a)),\n    }''')\nsrc = src.replace('''    participant_id = pm.Data(\"participant_id\"''', '''    seq_len = pm.Data(\"seq_len\", np.ones(1, dtype=\"float64\"))\n    participant_id = pm.Data(\"participant_id\"''')\nsrc = src.replace('''    theta = ideal[participant_id]''', '''    # Personal working-memory capacity in flips (non-centred log-normal population).\n    mu_cap = pm.Normal(\"mu_cap\", mu=np.log(6.0), sigma=0.7)\n    sigma_cap = pm.HalfNormal(\"sigma_cap\", sigma=0.7)\n    z_cap = pm.Normal(\"z_cap\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0, shape=MAX_PARTICIPANTS)\n    capacity = pm.Deterministic(\"capacity\", pm.math.exp(mu_cap + sigma_cap * z_cap))\n\n    theta = ideal[participant_id]''')\nsrc = src.replace('''    p_engaged = pm.math.sigmoid(score_a - score_b)''', '''    blur = pt.sqrt(1.0 + pt.sqr(seq_len / capacity[participant_id]))\n    p_engaged = pm.math.sigmoid((score_a - score_b) / blur)''')\nopen(\"iter_2/candidate_0/candidate.py\", \"w\").write(src)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"seq_len\\|blur\\|cap\" $D/candidate.py | head -20\ncd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/runs/run1/repo && /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -m src.pipelines.inner_loop.check_candidate --candidate-dir /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/iter_2/candidate_0 --responses /scratch/users/kushi